/P 88 0 R
/E (By the mid-19th century, the profession has transitioned from clerkship status to a regulated profession. In 1848, the Institute of Actuaries was established in London, followed by the Faculty of Actuaries in Edinburgh in 1856. Structured examinations were introduced and the foundations for the modern actuarial profession were set.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
221 0 obj
<<
