/P 91 0 R
/E (Architecting Resilience in an Age of Volatility)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (If the first three centuries of the actuarial profession were defined by calculating certainty, the next 25 years may be defined by navigating volatility. Modern times have brought around innovations that unfold at a pace and scale that outstrips anything experienced in previous centuries, - meaning past experience, while valuable, is an increasingly imperfect guide to what lies ahead.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (To answer why the world needs more actuaries, we must look at how the profession is evolving across three distinct landscapes: the global stage, the African frontier, and the local context.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (The AI Auditor)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (In a world where underwriting models are often powered by complex machine-learning systems, transparency becomes critical. Algorithms can unintentionally introduce bias by relying on hidden correlations related to geography, income, or other socio-economic factors.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Actuaries will play an essential role in reviewing and governing these systems  ensuring that models are not only efficient but also fair, transparent, and financially sound.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
