/E (The Demographic Conundrum)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (With a fertility rate well below replacement levels, the ratio of workers to pensioners is shrinking. The Mauritian actuary of 2040 will be tasked with redesigning the retirement frameworks - moving from static retirement ages toward "Health-Longevity" hybrids that ensure the national pension system remains solvent without sacrificing the welfare of the elderly.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Africa represents the most significant growth opportunity for the profession. Currently, less than 3% of the African population is covered by insurance, leaving a massive protection gap that threatens continental stability)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Inclusive Innovation)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Innovation is also emerging in how insurance products are designed. Parametric insurance, for example, allows payouts to be triggered automatically when predefined conditions  such as rainfall levels or wind speeds are met. Using satellite data and objective measurements, these products can deliver rapid financial support to smallholder farmers and communities affected by droughts or floods, bypassing lengthy claims processes. For many parts of Africa, such solutions may become a cornerstone of climate resilience.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (While global and regional developments shape the profession, Mauritius faces its own unique challenges.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The Blue Economy and Exported Expertise)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (At the same time, Mauritius continues to strengthen its position as an international financial centre. Actuaries begin modelling the risks of the Blue Economy - from renewable energy to sustainable aquaculture - providing the risk frameworks necessary for these new industries to attract global investment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The world does not simply need more actuaries to solve the problems of the past. It needs a profession capable of navigating an increasingly complex and uncertain future. From the first fire insurer established in Port Louis in 1854 to the algorithm-driven financial systems of tomorrow, the underlying mandate remains the same: to provide the stability that allows economies and societies to grow.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
